{"purpose":"Establish future-facing domain boundaries: Project → Artifact → Deployment → Server Runtime with dependency downward only and context isolation.","content":"PRD-001 Amendment 002: Four-Domain Architecture. Document ID PRD-001-AM-002, date 2026-07-25, status Accepted for future planning, effective Sprint 7+. Formalizes four-domain architecture without modifying historical PRD. Requirements: Project domain (requires anvil.yaml, repo-aware, never accesses Registry/State); Artifact domain (immutable payload, manifest.json authoritative, identity independent of filename); Deployment domain (transports/orchestrates between contexts, must not inspect Registry/layout, wrapper requesting Runtime operations); Server Runtime domain (owns Registry, State, installation, lifecycle, activation/rollback, locks/health; must not depend on repos/CI/transport; State includes immutable Artifact Store; reconciles after interrupts); CLI contexts (Development, Deployment, Server bridging via published Runtime commands). Traceability ADR-015, 004-four-domain-architecture.md, AM-001. See docs/prd/PRD-001-amendment-002-four-domain-architecture.md."}